From f4e7989e62e11b9433fec7284347343fbf7dcb78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Sugiyama <yuichis@ricsec.co.jp>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:29:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pta: veraison_attestation: take lifecycle and boot
 signer from i.MX fuses

The security lifecycle in the PSA token was a fixed test value, and
nothing described who signed the boot images. Add
CFG_VERAISON_ATTESTATION_PTA_PLATFORM_CLAIMS to take both from the
platform; the only implementation for now is the i.MX 8M family with
CFG_IMX_OCOTP=y:

- the lifecycle follows the fuses NXP's U-Boot consults to tell whether
  the HAB secure boot is in force: no SRK hash is "assembly and test",
  an SRK hash on an open device is "PSA RoT provisioning", a closed
  device, which only boots signed images, is "secured", and a closed
  device put in the field return state, which boots anything again, is
  "decommissioned";

- the boot signer is the SRK hash, the hash of the keys the HAB verifies
  the boot images against, read from the OCOTP fuses and returned in the
  byte order of the srktool efuse file (the fuses hold it as
  little-endian words). The next commit uses it for the TAs that are
  part of the core image.

The fuse map is the 8M family's, so the option is refused on other
i.MX parts. Without the option the token is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/OP-TEE/optee_os/pull/8109]
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Sugiyama <yuichis@ricsec.co.jp>
